而且我刚被周六夜现场解雇。

460
00:19:33.280 --> 00:19:34.740
I was like, how am I going to get a job?
当时我在想，我以后怎么找工作啊？

461
00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:37.260
And then they were like, there's this movie, Alvin and the Chipmunks.
然后他们就说，有这么一部电影，叫《鼠来宝》。

462
00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:38.460
I'm like, cool, great.
我说，行，太棒了。

463
00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:43.540
And then I'd never also worked with like a green screen or any special effects.
而且我以前也从没和绿幕或任何特效合作过。

464
00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:46.100
And like the Chipmunks aren't there.
而且花栗鼠根本不在现场。

465
00:19:46.300 --> 00:19:46.500
Right.
对。

466
00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:48.820
They're not real.
它们不是真的。

467
00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:53.400
And it already was like a sensitive time in my life because I was like, you know, like,
那本来就是我人生中一个比较敏感的时期，因为我在想，你知道的，

468
00:19:53.460 --> 00:19:54.680
am I ever going to act again?
我以后还能演戏吗？

469
00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:55.420
Like what happened?
到底怎么回事？

470
00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:58.820
And then I just like making the movie was genuinely very fun.
然后我就觉得拍电影本身其实真的非常有趣。

471
00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:04.380
And it was a lot of me in like a studio in Vancouver talking to like a tennis ball on the
我大部分时间都是在温哥华的一个录音棚里，对着一根棍子上的

472
00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:04.560
stick.
网球说话。

473
00:20:05.440 --> 00:20:07.340
I hope that doesn't show in the performance.
希望这在表演中没看出来。

474
00:20:07.340 --> 00:20:08.500
No, not at all.
没有，一点也没有。

475
00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:09.900
You totally sell it.
你完全演出来了。

476
00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:15.880
And then we had like a few weeks in Hawaii and my parents came to visit just to make sure
然后我们在夏威夷呆了几周，我父母来看望我，只是为了确保

477
00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:16.840
that I was like, okay.
我一切都好。

478
00:20:17.880 --> 00:20:18.640
Well, you got it.
好吧，你赚到了。

479
00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:23.840
You got a free trip out of Hawaii out of it, which is always fun when a movie or a project
你因此得到了一次免费的夏威夷之旅，当一部电影或一个项目

480
00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:24.840
takes you somewhere cool.
带你去一些酷炫的地方时，总是很有趣的。

481
00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:25.440
I know.
我知道。

482
00:20:25.600 --> 00:20:26.040
Oh yeah.
哦，对。

483
00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:27.640
God, that's such a plus.
天哪，这太棒了。

484
00:20:27.860 --> 00:20:28.900
It's all a dream.
这一切都像一场梦。

485
00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:34.420
Like, I don't know what your experience of being in the entertainment industry is,
就像，我不知道你在娱乐行业的经历是怎样的，

486
00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:36.560
but like, for me, it just has not worn off.
但对我来说，这种新鲜感真的没有消退。

487
00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:40.160
It just hasn't worn off that I'm like, this is so cool.
那种觉得“这太酷了”的感觉一点都没消退。

488
00:20:40.520 --> 00:20:40.720
Yeah.
对。

489
00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:41.360
Yeah.
对。

490
00:20:42.040 --> 00:20:44.560
Well, you've done so many things, Jenny.
珍妮，你做过的事情太多了。

491
00:20:44.740 --> 00:20:48.880
I mean, you are an actress, but you're also a comedian, but you've also written books,
我的意思是，你是一名演员，但你也是个喜剧演员，你还写过书，

492
00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:51.000
but you also are now a podcaster.
而且你现在还是个播客主。

493
00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:52.580
I'm very curious.
我很好奇。

494
00:20:53.220 --> 00:20:54.500
Take me back to the beginning.
带我回到最初吧。

495
00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:55.900
Like, where did you grow up?
你在哪里长大的？

496
00:20:56.000 --> 00:20:59.520
And at what point did you realize I want to be an entertainer?
你是在什么时候意识到“我想成为一名艺人”的？

497
00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:03.560
Well, I'm from Milton, Massachusetts, which is six miles south of Boston.
嗯，我来自马萨诸塞州的米尔顿，那是波士顿以南六英里远的地方。

498
00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:06.160
And that's where my family is from.
我的家人就住在那里。

499
00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:08.620
And I have two sisters.
我有两个姐妹。

500
00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:10.900
My parents are both artists.
我父母都是艺术家。

501
00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:13.640
My mom is a potter and my dad is a poet.
我妈妈是个陶艺家，我爸爸是个诗人。

502
00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:16.560
And we would like rent movies from the library.
我们会去图书馆借电影来看。

503
00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:22.360
You know, like one of my dad's friends got us a VCR and we rented movies from the library.
你知道的，比如我爸爸有个朋友给我们弄了一台录像机，我们就去图书馆借电影。

504
00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:25.540
And I really can't remember a time that I didn't want to be an actor.
我真的记不清从什么时候起，我就一直想成为一名演员。

505
00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.060
I really, really wanted to.
我是真的、真的很想。

506
00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:33.320
And a lot of that was based off of watching like Judy Garland and Gene Kelly, but like also
这很大程度上是因为看了朱迪·加兰和吉恩·凯利的电影，但也包括

507
00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:35.600
Sesame Street movies, like Follow That Bird.
《芝麻街》电影，比如《跟随那只鸟》。

508
00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:38.040
If anyone remembers that movie, it was so good.
如果有人还记得那部电影，它真的很棒。

509
00:21:38.200 --> 00:21:43.380
And like Shirley Temple, which I'm not sure those films have aged well, and I'm not sure
还有秀兰·邓波儿的电影，虽然我不确定那些电影是不是经得起时间考验，也不确定

510
00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:44.580
I could recommend them.
我能不能推荐它们。

511
00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:48.320
Maybe not the most sensitive, appropriate films anymore.
现在看来可能已经不是那么敏感、合适的电影了。

512
00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:52.400
But at the time, it was like mostly I just like that she was a little girl and she had
但在当时，我主要是喜欢她是个小女孩，穿着

513
00:21:52.400 --> 00:21:54.500
tap shoes and she like had a big lollipop.
踢踏舞鞋，还拿着一颗大棒棒糖。

514
00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:59.260
And I just, yeah, I always wanted to be a performer, but my parents, they were like,
我就是，对啊，我一直想成为一名表演者，但我父母他们的态度是，

515
00:21:59.320 --> 00:22:00.100
you can do that in school.
你可以在学校里搞这个。

516
00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:01.520
Like you can be in the plays and stuff.
比如你可以演演话剧什么的。

517
00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:02.680
And I did speech team.
我还参加了演讲队。

518
00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:06.920
I was on our speech and debate team, but they were just like, you're not going to do that
我加入了我们的演讲与辩论队，但他们就是觉得，在你上大学之前

519
00:22:06.920 --> 00:22:08.060
until you go to college.
你别想去干那个。

520
00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:09.400
It was kind of understood.
这基本上是默认的。

521
00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:13.480
And I didn't really realize like that there were tracks, you know, like this person is
而且我当时并不太懂原来还有不同的路线，你知道的，比如这个人

522
00:22:13.480 --> 00:22:15.500
a comedian or this person does dramatic acting.
是个喜剧演员，或者这个人演正剧。

523
00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:22.800
I kind of like thought you could just do everything because there also were actors that did that,
我当时觉得你什么都能演，因为确实也有演员能做到这一点，

524
00:22:22.800 --> 00:22:25.160
like Carol Burnett, for example.
比如卡罗尔·伯内特。

525
00:22:25.560 --> 00:22:27.900
Like I just like, I really loved her so much.
我当时就是，真的超级喜欢她。

526
00:22:28.000 --> 00:22:32.140
And for me, like her playing Miss Hannigan in Annie was like really scary.
对我来说，看她在《安妮》里扮演汉尼根小姐真的挺吓人的。

527
00:22:32.320 --> 00:22:32.660
Yeah.
对。

528
00:22:32.840 --> 00:22:33.620
And really dramatic.
而且非常有戏剧张力。

529
00:22:33.880 --> 00:22:36.780
And yeah, it never occurred to me that you might have to separate it out.
是的，我从来没想过你可能得把它们分开。

530
00:22:36.900 --> 00:22:40.660
And one of my life's dreams was to be on Saturday Night Live.
我人生的梦想之一就是登上《周六夜现场》。

531
00:22:40.660 --> 00:22:45.420
I watched like all the tapes of Gilda Radner and I was obsessed with Gilda Radner.
我看过吉尔达·拉德纳的所有录像带，我迷恋极了吉尔达·拉德纳。

532
00:22:45.420 --> 00:22:47.040
And I went to Columbia.
我上了哥伦比亚大学。

533
00:22:47.720 --> 00:22:50.900
I graduated and started doing standup with my best friend, Gabe Liedman.
我毕业后开始和我的好朋友盖布·利德曼一起表演单口喜剧。

534
00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:53.300
And that's like kind of how my career started.
我的职业生涯大概就是这么开始的。

535
00:22:53.500 --> 00:22:55.920
Like I got a manager who helped me get commercials.
我找了个经纪人，他帮我接拍广告。

536
00:22:56.160 --> 00:22:57.880
What was one of your earliest commercials?
你最早拍的广告之一是什么？

537
00:22:58.160 --> 00:22:59.260
Because that was my route.
因为我当年也是走这条路的。

538
00:22:59.400 --> 00:23:00.540
I did tons of commercials.
我拍了成吨的广告。

539
00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:03.100
And so I love seeing people in old commercials.
所以我特别喜欢看别人演的旧广告。

540
00:23:03.520 --> 00:23:04.960
First of all, I didn't book a lot.
首先，我其实没拿到多少广告。

541
00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:10.680
Did you ever book those that were called like industrial?
你演过那种被称为企业宣传片的吗？

542
00:23:10.980 --> 00:23:11.260
Oh, yeah.
哦，演过。

543
00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:11.760
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

544
00:23:11.760 --> 00:23:20.180
I did one for like, I think it was for Ford and I had to talk about like the, I don't
我拍过一个，好像是为福特拍的，我得讲解那个，我不知道，就是发动机里的某个东西，我当时

545
00:23:20.180 --> 00:23:24.520
know, it was something in the engine and it was like, I was so bad.
表现得太差劲了。

546
00:23:24.740 --> 00:23:25.940
It was really bad.
真的糟透了。

547
00:23:26.740 --> 00:23:27.140
Yeah.
对啊。

548
00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:31.480
I mean, I feel like commercials are genuinely very hard and you have to be like so normal
我的意思是，我觉得拍广告真的非常难，你经常必须表现得

549
00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:33.340
often about something that's not very exciting.
极其自然去推销一个其实没那么让人兴奋的东西。

550
00:23:33.540 --> 00:23:37.560
You know, like it's one thing if you're like, you're you as you endorsing a toothbrush
你知道的，如果你是以本色代言牙刷那还是一回事

551
00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:39.220
that you actually use, which I have done.
你真正会用的那种，而我已经用过了。

552
00:23:39.340 --> 00:23:40.480
And I'm like, I love this toothbrush.
然后我就想，我太喜欢这把牙刷了。

553
00:23:40.480 --> 00:23:43.740
I really like it for my teeth as Jenny.
作为珍妮，我真的很喜欢它来刷牙。

554
00:23:43.940 --> 00:23:47.080
But like, I remember doing a Cascade commercial.
不过，我记得我拍过一个 Cascade 洗碗机洗涤剂的广告。

555
00:23:47.620 --> 00:23:49.040
That's the one I really remember.
那是令我印象最深刻的一个。

556
00:23:49.280 --> 00:23:52.940
And that for reasons that I'll never understand, they gave me super long extensions.
而且原因不明，他们给我接了超长的头发。

557
00:23:53.080 --> 00:24:00.200
And also, I didn't have a dishwasher, you know, like a tiny apartment in Brooklyn.
而且当时我没有洗碗机，你知道的，就像布鲁克林的一间小公寓那样。

558
00:24:00.360 --> 00:24:00.980
I didn't have a dishwasher.
我没有洗碗机。

559
00:24:01.240 --> 00:24:05.080
And like the one I had used was like my parents dishwasher.
我以前用过的唯一洗碗机是我父母家的那种。

560
00:24:05.620 --> 00:24:07.080
Like that was very old.
就像那种非常旧的。

561
00:24:07.220 --> 00:24:09.660
And I didn't like I'd never used like a pod before.
而且我以前从没用过像洗碗块这样的东西。

562
00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:12.360
I just I remember the whole day being like, I am so busted.
我只记得那一整天我都觉得自己要露馅了。

563
00:24:12.560 --> 00:24:14.060
Like, I don't know how to do this.
就像，我根本不知道该怎么做。

564
00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:16.940
That's amazing.
太神奇了。

565
00:24:17.420 --> 00:24:17.660
Yeah.
是啊。

566
00:24:17.860 --> 00:24:20.440
But it was a good way to make money while I was doing standup.
但这是我在做单口喜剧期间赚钱的一个好方法。

567
00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:25.440
And my first audition for anything I believe that I got was the show Bored to Death, which
我得到的第一个试镜机会好像是电视剧《凡人烦人》，

568
00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:29.080
starred Jason Schwartzman and Ted Danson and Zach Galifianakis.
由詹森·舒瓦兹曼、特德·丹森和扎克·加利费安纳基斯主演。

569
00:24:29.080 --> 00:24:31.980
And that was like my first job.
那就像是我的第一份工作。

570
00:24:32.720 --> 00:24:33.200
Wow.
哇。

571
00:24:33.740 --> 00:24:34.140
Yeah.
是啊。

572
00:24:34.380 --> 00:24:41.780
So at that time, like Jason Schwartzman and Ted Danson were Ted Danson and Jason Schwartzman.
所以在当时，詹森·舒瓦兹曼和特德·丹森就已经大名鼎鼎了。

573
00:24:41.900 --> 00:24:44.240
But Zach Galifianakis was still kind of coming up, right?
但扎克·加利费安纳基斯当时还算是在上升期，对吧？

574
00:24:44.720 --> 00:24:49.480
Yeah, I believe it was the year before the hangover one came out.
对，我记得那是《宿醉》上映前的一年。

575
00:24:49.660 --> 00:24:49.860
Yeah.
是啊。

576
00:24:50.400 --> 00:24:50.780
Yeah.
对。

577
00:24:51.220 --> 00:24:52.300
So I'm just curious.
所以我很好奇。

578
00:24:52.300 --> 00:24:54.200
I've worked with a few of those guys.
我和其中几位合作过。

579
00:24:54.880 --> 00:24:56.140
And they're so talented.
他们太有才华了。

580
00:24:56.540 --> 00:24:58.560
And you walk on the set, like, what was that like?
你走进片场时，那种感觉是什么样的？

581
00:24:59.080 --> 00:24:59.580
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

582
00:25:00.340 --> 00:25:01.560
I would definitely remember.
我绝对记得。

583
00:25:01.720 --> 00:25:06.120
Because first of all, my best friend is married to Zach.
因为首先，我最好的朋友嫁给了扎克。

584
00:25:07.020 --> 00:25:12.500
And I didn't tell them that I was auditioning for the show because I just felt embarrassed.
而且我没有告诉他们我要去试镜这部剧，因为我觉得很尴尬。

585
00:25:12.640 --> 00:25:15.420
First of all, I don't really like asking for favors, I guess.
首先，我猜我其实不太喜欢开口求人。

586
00:25:15.560 --> 00:25:16.080
I juSt...
我只是……

587
00:25:16.080 --> 00:25:16.840
And I don't know.
而且我不知道。

588
00:25:17.000 --> 00:25:17.940
Like, what if I was bad?
万一我表现得很糟糕呢？

589
00:25:18.080 --> 00:25:20.660
And then I'm not sure they could have helped me get on the show.
而且我不确定他们能不能帮我得到这个角色。

590
00:25:20.740 --> 00:25:21.360
But I just like...
但我只是觉得……

591
00:25:21.360 --> 00:25:23.620
I was like, oh, I got this part.
我就想，哦，我拿到这个角色了。

592
00:25:23.740 --> 00:25:27.240
Now I actually have to tell them weirdly that I'm like showing up at Zach's job.
现在我竟然得怪异地告诉他们，我要去扎克工作的剧组了。

593
00:25:27.240 --> 00:25:32.600
And it was like, it was supposed to be only like, I was going to play this cashier and
而且当时本来应该只是，我只是去演这个收银员，

594
00:25:32.600 --> 00:25:33.780
it was a smaller part.
那是个小角色。

595
00:25:33.920 --> 00:25:37.800
And then they made it bigger because it actually was so fun and went very well, which is like
然后他们把戏份加重了，因为效果真的很好玩也很顺利，这简直是

596
00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:38.940
kind of every actor's dream.
每个演员的梦想。

597
00:25:39.140 --> 00:25:45.580
But I just remember like, you know, I was a huge Jason fan and I'm from Boston.
但我只记得，你知道的，我是詹森的超级粉丝，而且我来自波士顿。

598
00:25:45.800 --> 00:25:47.060
Like Ted Danson, cheers.
就像特德·丹森的《干杯》。

599
00:25:47.240 --> 00:25:48.020
I mean, yeah.
我是说，对。

600
00:25:48.020 --> 00:25:49.600
It's just crazy.
这简直太疯狂了。

601
00:25:49.900 --> 00:25:55.120
And I just remember being like, just don't say anything.
我只记得当时心里在想，什么都别说。

602
00:25:55.360 --> 00:25:57.400
Just don't do anything.
什么都别做。

603
00:25:57.720 --> 00:25:58.520
Don't say anything.
什么也别说。

604
00:25:58.880 --> 00:26:00.040
Just do your lines.
只管念你的台词就行。

605
00:26:00.240 --> 00:26:03.380
And like, just don't be weird, you know?
而且，就别表现得那么奇怪，你知道吧？

606
00:26:03.580 --> 00:26:06.120
And that plan, which is like a terrible plan.
而那个计划，简直是个糟糕透顶的计划。

607
00:26:06.260 --> 00:26:08.640
I don't even know what that says about what I thought of myself.
我甚至不知道这说明了我当时是怎么看自己的。

